# The Linux list: the check line's commands assigned to Linux, one id a line (`share.sh ids` names every
# command's id). Read by share.sh, so the PR check's Linux share (check-linux.yml), the twin's matrix
# (check.yml's `suite` jobs), the macOS share and the rest all split the line by this one file.
# CircleCI's static matrix (.circleci/parts/check-linux.yml) must list the same ids: share.sh fails
# when it differs. An id joins once its suite passes on Linux (.circleci/linux-local.sh reproduces one
# on a Mac). wharf-runs' check.sh is one command of the line and ten `wharf-runs-<shard>` ids here
# (share.sh reads its --list-shards); eight passed on Linux (#500, 2026-11-05) and are here (pickup left it
# for a day, until the self-hosted runners had lsof: runner-lsof, 2026-11-06). Off this
# list: sextant and wharf-runs-macos, whose suites need macOS, and wharf-runs-queue, whose finish-queue cases
# read a Mac's claim and memory floors. A wharf-runs shard joins with its suites on check.sh's LINUX_OK, in one change.
